\image(figures/forecast_baselines.svg)
// result_end

The first-origin plot illustrates a single trajectory. The lead-wise
average combines all origins and is the basis for comparing methods.

The difference recurrence leads at horizons one through four. Seasonal
naive has the lowest error at leads five and six. The recursive model's
error grows as more of its own predicted differences enter the lag window.

> References

- [Hyndman and Athanasopoulos, Simple forecasting methods|https://otexts.com/fpp3/simple-methods.html].
- [Hyndman and Athanasopoulos, ARIMA models|https://otexts.com/fpp3/arima.html].
